+Each entry carries `cardId`, `fixtureId`, `teamId`, `shownOn`, `matches`, `served`,
+`outstanding`, `servedIn` (fixture ids in order) and `clearedOn` (the day the last match was
+served, else `null`). Only cards worth at least one match have entries.
+
+A ban is served over played games of the side the card was shown for: only a game with status
+`played` serves a match; `awarded`, `postponed` and `abandoned` games serve nothing. Each played
+game serves one match off the earliest outstanding card shown to that side before it. Rescinded
+cards drop out and any games they had been allocated fall through to later cards.
+
+`suspended` is `true` while any match is outstanding.
+
+### `GET /fixtures/:fixtureId/eligibility`
+Takes no query fields. Reads the record as of the day before the fixture. Answers `fixtureId`,
+`playedOn`, `asOf` and `ineligible`: every registered player at either club who has a match
+outstanding as of that day. Home side first, then by player id. Each entry carries `playerId`,
+`clubId`, `teamId` (their side in this game) and `outstanding`.
 
